Universal workflow rules: ~/.claude/rules/workflow.md (execution honesty,
scope discipline, end-of-session review, handoff protocol). Read with this file.
Hard controls: ~/.claude/hooks/guard.py (PreToolUse) blocks .env edits,
live-mode toggles (DRY_RUN/TESTNET=false, --live), prod `supabase db reset/push`,
Supabase MCP apply_migration, and root-level rm -rf. A block means: stop and ask
{{APPROVER}}, except the two self-fixable rules: 5 (self-matching `pgrep -f` wait
loop) and 6 (an unquoted $var that needs word-splitting; zsh does not split, so the
command silently acts on nothing and still exits 0). For both: fix it and rerun.
If ~/.claude/RULE_SYNC_DRIFT.md exists: standing rules have diverged.
Resolve it (instructions inside) before other work.

